# Feedback

Tell people where their feedback goes before they write it, and confirm receipt only when a real response says it arrived. Collecting a page response is separate from contacting support or reporting an urgent problem.

**Reference pattern.** The examples document a local adaptation. They do not add a publishing backend or a new Home Assistant capability.

## Use the shared delivery contract

[Feedback](../../components/feedback.html#usage) owns destination disclosure, privacy, retained input and confirmed or uncertain delivery. This page keeps the local form and the real issue-route examples. Neither installs a feedback service in Home Assistant.

## When to use it

For Civica documentation, give a clear route to report a documentation problem or suggest an improvement, and say that a public issue may be visible to others. In the Home Assistant interface, use the existing support path for the affected integration.

## Structure and behaviour

Label each field. Show confirmation only after a real successful response. Keep typed text available after a failure. Make an email address optional unless the service needs it, and explain why before asking.

## Home Assistant boundary

The examples acknowledge activity locally and send nothing. They install no analytics, survey endpoint, notification service or email collection. Never describe a local demonstration as a submitted report.

## Local feedback interaction

Type invented feedback. The demonstration does not send or save it.

